A||||16||sjp777||What is the deal with 88 calipers?||||8||
Z||000000||sjp777||06-20-2001||08:47 PM||||Ok, about this time last year I had a caliper freeze up, so I bought a rebuild from the local parts store.<P>A couple months ago I got my new rims which really show the calipers that looked like crap with dirt and corrosion.<P>I got out my drill and wire wheel bit and went to town. Afterwards I used a small buffing wheel and some metal polish.<P>This made them all very shiny and they looked killer with the rims. The first time I washed the car, within minutes the caliper that I had replaced turned orange with rust. The other 3 are still shiny to this day.<P>I figured the rebuild was an aftermarket done in steel since the original alloy shouldn't rust. I found a guy on this forum who had an outer half of an original caliper. I bought and it came today. It's painted black, is pretty heavy, and a magnet will stick to it. I figured I got another steel one right? But then I did the magnet test on the originals and the magnets stick to those as well, yet they don't rust so they must be alloy.<P>Before I go through the hassle of stripping the paint and polishing the half I got today, does anyone know what is up with the 88 calipers and would I be wasting my time?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||cadaver||06-21-2001||02:42 AM||||They could be nitrited or cad plated I dont know without looking at one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||06-21-2001||02:43 AM||||Take them off and chrome them||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||06-21-2001||10:52 AM||||There will be no chrome on my car. Yuck.<P>No one knows?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||06-21-2001||11:19 AM||||I'd say polish them up again, and then paint them with some high temp clear paint to protect them from moisture. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||06-21-2001||12:36 PM||||Total guess but some sort of stainless steel alloy would be magnetic and not rust... Mine must be like your 3, they were dirty but not rusted. I painted them red so I don't know for sure what they would do if polished though.||||reg||5
Z||000006||88formula||06-21-2001||05:02 PM||||Half of my original 88 two piece Calipers are cast iron. They are painted black at the factory and probably have some kind of protective coating on them as well. When a caliper gets remanufactured they usually get sand blasted or bead blasted to remove corrosion and the protective paint gets wiped out. That’s why the rebuilt one rusted and the original one's didn't.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||sjp777||06-21-2001||09:08 PM||||except for the fact that all got the wire wheel treatment down to bare metal before the polish.<P>I don't know why the one rusted and others didn't||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||06-21-2001||09:29 PM||||???||||reg||1
Z||000009||88 Database Guy||06-21-2001||09:45 PM||||I've been wondering about this too.  I got some '88 calipers from a junkyard thinking I'd clean and refurb them back to as-new for my future show car.  Well, after cleaning the first one with brass wool and other stuff, I've stripped off the color from the outer section.  The inner section, with the piston in it, is definately painted grey.<P>Another of the calipers was very clean and required nothing more than a few good scrubbings with "Simple Green".  THAT caliper looks like new, and the outer part DEFINATELY looks plated.  It's not paint, that's for sure.  The stripped one looks like an aluminum alloy, but I never thought of the magnet test, I'll do that tomorrow.<P>So, does anyone have any info on the grey paint on the piston half of the calipers and the coating on the outer half?  The coating or plating has a golden metallic tint, is that cadmium plating?||||reg||1
Z||000010||qwikgta||06-21-2001||10:25 PM||||I know this has nothing to do with 88 brakes (I too wire brushed mine, no rust yet) but I got a DUKE intake manifold off an 87 and I cleaned it all up.  90% is shinny aluminum but on one end the mani is gold color.  It won't rub off its like its two diff metals in one.  So again this doesn't help but I still can't figure it out either.<P><BR>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000011||cadaver||06-22-2001||12:27 AM||||So let me get this straight. You will try to polish steel to get nice and bright but you wont chrome anything? Hmmmm. You could always nickel plate them. That has a real rich look.||||reg||1
Z||000012||sjp777||06-22-2001||12:57 AM||||I thought I was polishing aluminum. It seems only the piston halves of the calipers are aluminum. I guess the outer halves are steel.<P>Why one rusts and the others don't is a great mystery.<P>Chrome is out. It would look way tacky with my silver rims.<P>I am going to try stripping the new half I got, polishing it, and see if it holds. If not, I'll take them all off and get them powder coated red.||||reg||1
Z||000013||ray b||06-22-2001||01:07 AM||||the duck manafold color is caused by heat<BR>ever see colors after a part is welded same thing caused it<BR>88 brakes if a magnet sticks it is not alum<BR>alum alloy will turn white or gray not rust red/orange color but brakes can discolor from heat to. use a high heat paint like header paint VTX was one brand name.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000014||cadaver||06-22-2001||09:46 PM||||so you wont chrome them because you think it tacky but you will try to polish them? And you will powder coat them and that wont be tacky?||||reg||1
Z||000015||sjp777||06-22-2001||10:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadaver:<BR><B>so you wont chrome them because you think it tacky but you will try to polish them? And you will powder coat them and that wont be tacky?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Since I seem to need to keep repeating myself.<P>Yes, I think chrome is tacky.<P>Polished metal: Not tacky<P>Red powder coat: Not tacky<P>On my car, only my opinion counts.<P>What you do to your car and what you think is cool is all that counts on your car.<P>I was just trying to find out what the friggin calipers are made of.||||reg||1
